Title:
Proteus — Rust Mythic C2 Agent (Polymorphic Shellcode)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Proteus is a Rust-based agent for the Mythic C2 framework that builds as raw, position-independent Windows x64 shellcode rather than a PE. It focuses on reducing static signatures by avoiding import tables (dynamic API resolution via PEB walking), encrypting embedded strings/data in custom `.rdata` sections using ChaCha20, and producing per-build structural variance through a function-shuffling linker pipeline. The repo includes three Rust crates (agent, COFF layout/relocation analyzer, and obfuscation runtime/proc-macros) plus a Python Mythic Payload Type service to integrate builds and commands into Mythic. The agent runs `no_std/no_main`, boots from a custom `_start`, allocates a private NT heap, and communicates over WinHTTP. It’s primarily useful for red teams/pentesters building Mythic operations and for researchers studying polymorphic build pipelines and shellcode-oriented agent design.

Technical Focus:
- Mythic Payload Type integration (Python MythicContainer SDK)
- Windows x64 shellcode agent design (`no_std`, `no_main`, custom `_start`)
- Dynamic API resolution via PEB walk (no static imports)
- COFF/REL32 relocation analysis and function reordering (shuffle pipeline)
- ChaCha20-encrypted data/strings in custom `.rdata` sections (proc-macro driven)
- WinHTTP-based C2 communications

Use Cases:
- Deploying a Mythic-compatible Windows shellcode agent in lab/red team engagements
- Generating per-build polymorphic payloads to test signature-based detections
- Studying/implementing COFF relocation repair for function shuffling
- Building string/data obfuscation via compile-time macros + runtime decrypt-on-use
- Creating a shellcode-only agent to be wrapped by a separate PE loader (e.g., Minotaur)

Keywords:
Mythic, C2 agent, Rust, shellcode, Windows x64, no_std, no_main, PEB walk, dynamic API resolution, WinHTTP, COFF, REL32, RIP-relative, linker script, function shuffling, polymorphic build, ChaCha20, data section obfuscation, proc-macro, .rdata sections